{"node":{"id":"HP:0012721","label":"Venous malformation","ic":6.897,"definition":"A vascular malformation resulting from a developmental error of venous tissue composed of dysmorphic channels lined by flattened endothelium and exhibiting slow turnover. A venous malformation may present as a blue patch on the skin ranging to a soft blue mass. Venous malformations are easily compressible and usually swell in thewhen venous pressure increases (e.g., when held in a dependent position or when a child cries). They may be relatively localized or quite extensive within an anatomic region."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0008318","label":"Proteus syndrome","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_1edd091ce9c7","source":"MONDO:0008318","target":"HP:0012721","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:176920 · OMIM:176920","url":"https://omim.org/entry/176920","level":"curated","date":"2014-08-03","confidence":0.5,"snippet":"Proteus syndrome, somatic: Venous malformation [TAS]"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:744 · ORPHA:744","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/744","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Proteus syndrome: Venous malformation (frequency HP:0040282) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:744","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/744","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Venous malformation — Frequent (79-30%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.6,"independent_sources":["OMIM","Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.6},{"id":"MONDO:0700325","label":"Parkes Weber syndrome","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_98d6218069f7","source":"MONDO:0700325","target":"HP:0012721","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:90307 · ORPHA:90307","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/90307","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Parkes Weber syndrome: Venous malformati